Looks a bit too hacky.  IMO, it's better to define a struct

	struct tas_codec {
		struct aoa_codec codec;
		struct tas *tas;
	}

to make the above simpler like:

	static struct tas *codec_to_tas(struct aoa_codec *codec)
	{
		return ((struct tas_codec *)codec)->tas;
	}

